Am I the only person that thinks Monks are one of the easiest classes
to ascend?  Healers aren't that bad either -- they are just painfully
slow to play in the first half of the game.

I think Priests are the hardest class.  All the other spellcasting
classes are guaranteed to start with at least one useful spellbook,
but the Priest gets to play the RNG lotto to see if he starts the game
with a useful spellbook.  Also, automatic B/U/C identifying isn't very
exciting, and their melee and ranged weapon selection is awful.  Their
starting weapon can rust, and they aren't very common to find.


